\par\par \b \uc2  Yen tumbles as  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  says  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  with NY Fed. \b0\par\par\uc2 301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2001\par 15:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  1336 GMT - Yen tumbles to fresh 2-week lows vs dollar, slides to new one-month troughs against euro after Senior Japanese finance ministry official Zembe Mizoguchi said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in U.S. trading, using the New York Federal Reserve as its agent. NY Fed, however, declines comment. \par \par \uc2  - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since last week to push yen lower, and earlier this week drafted the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to act on its behalf. Earlier, ECB declines comment. \par \par \uc2  - Dollar/yen edges off fresh session highs near 120, changes hands around 119.80 yen , up more than 1.70 percent on the day after BOJ interevenes repeatedly overnight to cap yen's export-crimping strength. \par \par \uc2  - Euro/yen also up more than a full percent on the day, as BOJ enlists ECB's help to weaken yen for the third time this week. Euro trades around 109.80 yen , not far from session highs below 110 yen. \par \par \uc2  - Euro/dollar hugs session troughs, hovers near 91.70 cents , down more than 0.60 percent on the day. \par \par \uc2  - Market snoozes at U.S. durable goods data for August, which falls 0.3 percent, below expectations for a 0.2 percent decrease. July data revised down to -1.1 percent fall. \par \par \uc2  - U.S. weekly jobless claims rise to 450,000 in Sept. 22 week from revised 392,000 in prior week, reach highest since July 25, 1992. The four-week average rose to 422,000 in the Sept. 22 week from the revised 410,000 in the prior week. \par \par \uc2  - Earlier ECB leaves European rates steady as its regular monetary policy meeting on Thursday, as had been expected after the ECB's intra-meeting cut alongside the U.S. Federal Reserve on September 17. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010927dx9r00py0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
