\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen driven lower by BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Natsuko Waki \par \uc2 828 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2001\par 13:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 27 (Reuters) - The yen fell to a two-week low against the dollar and one-month trough against the euro after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the third time this week to halt export-damaging yen strength. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed the Bank of Japan bought dollars for yen in Tokyo and European trading, pushing Thursday's European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest rate decision out of the market's main focus. \par \par \uc2  The ECB confirmed it and the euro zone central banks were buying euros against the yen on behalf of the BOJ for the third day this week. \par \par \uc2  "What the BOJ has been doing for this week is to try to let the market know they are ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and they have been quite successful," Henry Wilkes, head of European \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  desk at Brown Brothers Harriman. \par \par \uc2  "Some market feeling is that the BOJ may not be finished until the dollar/yen goes up above 120. So the market is definitely nervous." \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose more than one percent against the yen to hit two-week highs around 119.38, off three percent from a seven-month low set last week. \par \par \uc2  Against the Swiss franc, it climbed to 1.6076 per dollar, around 2.5 percent above last week's 20-month trough. \par \par \uc2  The euro bounded to a one-month high against the yen of 109.89 from the New York close around 108.62. The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was one third of a percent up on the Swiss franc at 1.4809 francs. \par \par \uc2  The euro was steady against the dollar ahead of the ECB's regular interest rate decision later in the day. Many economists expect no change. \par \par \uc2  The Swiss franc fell against the euro and the dollar, retracing some of its hefty rise on safe-haven flows following the attacks on the U.S. on September 11. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  CAUTION \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is battling to restrain the yen in order to prevent deflationary pressure from worsening and to help domestic manufacturers at a time when the economy risks tipping into a recession. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say a weaker yen could be a boost to exports. It is also one of the few viable options for action by the Japanese authorities, given their limited scope in terms of fiscal and monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  Vice Finance Minister Toshiro Muto said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  because it feared the yen's surge could harm prospects for economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  "The market knows they are determined. Some speculators are positioning themselves expecting more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , going long on dollars," a European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Despite the BOJ's effort, general sentiment on the dollar remained frail with the Dow Jones industrial average falling 1.1 percent on Wednesday as warnings about corporate earnings snapped a two-day relief rally. \par \par \uc2  The International Monetary Fund said on Wednesday U.S. economic growth was skidding lower before the September 11 attacks and now it was impossible to predict what would happen. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa did admit yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was having limited impact. "The top side (in dollar/yen) is heavy and it hasn't broken through it. On the other hand, it is not going down either," Shiokawa told a government panel. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said repatriation flows by Japanese investors ahead of half-year book closing in September have almost dried up, which has removed one factor to drive the yen higher. \par \par \uc2  Many cash-rich Japanese institutional investors were trying to make decisions on what they should do with their money in the second half of the fiscal year, with some looking for an opportunity to buy U.S. dollar-denominated bonds, traders said. \par \par \uc2  They said investors were showing interest in buying U.S. bonds of maturities of between two and five years but looking for more clues on the U.S. economic outlook and interest rates. \par \par \uc2  ECB RATE DECISION \par \par \uc2  The ECB's regular monetary policy meeting is expected to make no change in interest rates after its intra-meeting cut alongside the U.S. Federal Reserve on September 17. The decision is due at 1145 GMT with no news conference scheduled. \par \par \uc2  Eurozone M3 money supply growth, which the ECB sees as a key barometer of future inflation, accelerated faster than expected in August to some two points above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 4.5 percent reference value. But analysts said persistent doubts about the reliability of the data mean its impact on the bank's monetary policy decision will be limited. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters expect the ECB to leave its benchmark minimum bid rate at 3.75 percent following a 50-basis point cut in reaction to the U.S. attacks on September 11. \par \par \uc2  But they do expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut rates again later this year as signs of gloom in the euro zone economy become more evident. \par \par \uc2  Later today, U.S. data due include weekly jobless claims and August durable goods orders at 1230 GMT. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010927dx9r00lly\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppic