\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar holds grounds vs yen, upside marred. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chisa Fujioka \par \uc2 592 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2001\par 05:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 27 (Reuters) - The dollar kept its edge over the yen on Thursday, clinging to gains racked up in offshore trade after Japan waded into the market again to restrain its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But the dollar failed to extend its rise, marred by uncertainties hanging over the fate of the U.S. economy in the wake of the September 11 aircraft attacks on U.S. cities. \par \par \uc2  Adding concern were U.S. shares snapping a two-day relief rally overnight on a flood of warnings about corporate earnings. \par \par \uc2  "There will be limits to a dollar rise... The likely recession in the U.S. economy and the impact on U.S. stocks aren't fully reflected in the market yet," said Masayuki Yamamoto, research analyst at Bank of America. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 117.74/79 yen in late morning, up modestly from 117.69 yen in late New York trade. It had earlier revisited offshore highs around 118.07, but was met with stiff offers there from exporters. \par \par \uc2  The yen also showed restraint against the euro, with the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 108.54/64 yen from a late offshore level of 108.62. Against the dollar, the euro stood at 92.20/25 cents from 92.30. \par \par \uc2  BOJ ACTS AGAIN \par \par \uc2  The yen was tamed overnight as the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ), under instruction from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a fifth time in two weeks. It was the second time it enlisted the help of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Japan has kept up a campaign to stem the yen's rise in an apparent bid to ease the pressure a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exerts on Japanese exporters. \par \par \uc2  Its determination was seen strong and many were wary of a possible repeat performance by the BOJ before the end of the fiscal half-year on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "The market is very cautious the BOJ may step in before the end of the fiscal half-year, possibly with the aim to bring the dollar up to 118 or even 119 yen," a Japanese bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  But few were betting on a stronger dollar, given the risk-averse mood as worries remained over how the U.S. would respond to the suicide aircraft attacks on New York and Washington. \par \par \uc2  Fears of a U.S. recession had also intensified on Tuesday after a report showed U.S. consumer confidence plunging in September. The number posed a threat to retail spending, one aspect of the economy that had held up amid overall sluggish growth. \par \par \uc2  SWISS FRANC \par \par \uc2  But despite jitters over imminent U.S. military action, the Swiss franc, a traditional safe-haven for worried investors, continued to shed its recent lustre. \par \par \uc2  Dealers have noted the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's desire to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively lowering interest rates by a full percentage point in September as it soared on safe-haven flows. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was around 1.5998/06 francs from 1.5990 in late offshore and more than three centimes better than Friday's 20-month lows. \par \par \uc2  Analysts, however, said the Swiss franc should remain well-supported as long as the possibility of U.S. retaliation for the attacks looked near. \par \par \uc2  Rising at the expense of the Swiss franc was the British pound, which climbed to near eight-month highs against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Helped by investors' switch into higher-yielding assets, sterling held overnight gains at $1.4750 At 4.75 percent, Britain's official interest rates are the highest in the Group of Seven leading industrial nations. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010927dx9r00e8j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
