\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro, dollar rise against yen after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Robin Shepherd \par \uc2 687 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2001\par 14:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 26 (Reuters) - The yen fell against the euro and the dollar on Wednesday after Japan once again stepped into the markets to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , enlisting the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as its agent for the second time this week. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, both the euro and the dollar pushed up by almost three quarters of a percent against the Swiss franc, itself hit by wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a general feeling that many investors have become extremely long in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Swiss franc has recently benefited from a flood of safe haven buying. \par \par \uc2  The dollar and the euro jumped half a yen, with the dollar hitting a one-week high, as Japan and the ECB confirmed they had been selling the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The yen has been strengthening recently as investors repatriate assets ahead of the fiscal half-year end this month and as risk aversion grows. \par \par \uc2  "The yen weakened. We've had confirmation from the BOJ and the ECB acting on its behalf," said Michael Metcalfe, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  eocnomist at Credit Agricole Indosuez. "But they're going to have to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  as long as these repatriation flows continue." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  began its current campaign to depress the yen more than a week ago, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on at least five separate days, across all time zones and twice with the assistance of the ECB. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose as high as 118.03 yen after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  before easing back to around 117.97 by 1200 GMT. The euro rose to just under 108.90 yen before slipping to 108.74. \par \par \uc2  The euro was steady against the dollar around $0.9225. The Swiss franc stood at 1.6027 to the dollar and 1.4787 to the euro. \par \par \uc2  SWISSIE LOSES GROUND \par \par \uc2  The Swiss franc was the biggest mover among major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , falling sharply against the euro and the dollar. Some analysts put this in the context of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "People think if the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  so aggressively then why wouldn't the Swiss National Bank come in as well," said Jesper Dannesboe, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Wasserstein in London. \par \par \uc2  He added that the Swiss National Bank had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets on Wednesday and that it was unlikely to do so. The BOJ moves had simply alerted people to the possibility that it might. \par \par \uc2  Other analysts agreed, while offering an alternative explanation for the Swiss franc's depreciation. \par \par \uc2  "I think it's the market being extremely long Swiss francs in a slightly more stable environment," said Audrey Childe-Freeman at CIBC World markets. \par \par \uc2  Generally, analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  should stay fairly well-supported as long as the threat of U.S. retaliation for the attacks on its cities remained. \par \par \uc2  REPATRIATION MIGHT BE DRYING UP \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Japan might find it easier to restrain upward pressure on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the close of business for the day as Wednesday is the last \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading day ahead of the interim, fiscal-book-closing on Friday. \par \par \uc2  As a rule, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  settlement takes place two business days after a transaction. \par \par \uc2  Otherwise, dealers said concern about possible coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Group of Seven was allayed after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance minister Masajuro Shiokawa said finance ministers from the seven richest countries did not discuss this in a teleconference on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  GLOOMY OUTLOOK \par \par \uc2  With little major economic news on the agenda, attention was turning to Friday's University of Michigan consumer sentiment index for further clues on the impact of the airplane attacks on U.S. consumer confidence. \par \par \uc2  U.S. credit rating company Standard & Poor's said on Wednesday that it saw the September 11 attacks pushing the United States into recession in the third and fourth quarters. \par \par \uc2  It also said chances were increasing of a sharper downgrade of Japan's sovereign credit rating within the AA category, signalling that it may cut the rating more than a notch from its current double A-plus (AA+). \par \par \uc2  The rating company put Japan on review for possible downgrade earlier this month. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926dx9q05wii\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
