\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar pares losses vs yen, BOJ comments help. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Dhara Ranasinghe \par \uc2 648 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2001\par 10:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 26 (Reuters) - The dollar pared early losses against the euro and yen on Wednesday, drawing support after comments from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor kept alive the prospect of further Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, sentiment towards the dollar remained bearish following news a day ago that U.S. consumer confidence suffered its worst fall in 11 years, according to a survey that captured part of the shock from the September 11 aeroplane attacks. \par \par \uc2  Still, the comments from BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami that it was not good for the dollar to fall were seen supporting the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near term. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times in the past week to cap yen strength. \par \par \uc2  "There are fears of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the backdrop," said Nick Stamenkovic, senior strategist at Noumura International. \par \par \uc2  "But sentiment is fragile and the consequences are the dollar will struggle, with the U.S. consumer confidence data suggesting the U.S. is in or on the edge of recession." \par \par \uc2  Yen-buying pressure was strong as Wednesday is effectively the last \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading day ahead of interim fiscal book-closings on Friday, dealers said. \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  settlement takes place two business days after a transaction. \par \par \uc2  Dealers were also nervous about selling the euro against the yen after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) acted on behalf of the BOJ on Monday when Japanese markets were closed for a holiday. \par \par \uc2  Japan is worried that a firm yen will dent an already frail doemstic economy. \par \par \uc2  At 0733 GMT, the dollar stood around 117.35, down a touch from late New York levels but more than a percent above seven-month troughs set last week. \par \par \uc2  The euro was little changed on the day around $0.9225 and 108.25 yen. \par \par \uc2  U.S DATA WATCH \par \par \uc2  With little major economic news on the agenda, attention was turning to Friday's University of Michigan consumer sentiment index for further clues on the impact of the airplane attacks on U.S. consumer confidence. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the U.S. Conference Board said its monthly index of consumer confidence dropped 16.4 points to 97.6 in September from a month earlier, much lower than analysts' forecasts. \par \par \uc2  The survey reflected only part of the shock of the attacks, which bodes ill for retail spending, which had been propping up the sluggish U.S. economy before the strikes. \par \par \uc2  Adding uncertainty were question marks over how Washington intends to retaliate for the assaults and what the economic impact of any action would be. \par \par \uc2  "Given that military action is imminent, there are growing risk factors facing U.S. assets," said Akihiro Nishida, chief economist at Tokyo-Mitsubishi Securities in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "But it's unclear whether there will be more repatriation from Japanese investors after the fiscal half-year end, since there aren't many attractive investment options at home." \par \par \uc2  GLOOMY OUTLOOK \par \par \uc2  U.S. credit rating company Standard & Poor's said on Wednesday that it saw the September 11 attacks pushing the United States into recession in the third and fourth quarters. \par \par \uc2  It also said chances were increasing of a sharper downgrade of Japan's sovereign credit rating within the AA category, signalling that it may cut the rating more than a notch from its current double A-plus (AA+). \par \par \uc2  The rating company put Japan's rating on a review for possible downgrade earlier this month. \par \par \uc2  Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke, meanwhile, was quoted as saying that the European economy stood a good chance of picking up in the fourth quarter and the attacks on the United States should not shake the foundations of the global economy. \par \par \uc2  Welteke, also a member of the ECB governing council, told Germany's Handelsblatt daily that the ECB's half-point rate cut last week aimed to boost confidence after the assaults on two U.S. cities. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926dx9q03xtl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
