\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar pressured, wariness over BOJ lends support. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 673 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2001\par 08:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 26 (Reuters) - The dollar edged down in Tokyo on Wednesday but found solid support around 117 yen amid wariness over possible further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and after a two-day winning streak on Wall Street. \par \par \uc2  But underlying sentiment for the greenback stayed weak amid lingering uncertainty over the impact of the September 11 attacks in the United States on its economy. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar was pressured but the market was very nervous about pushing the dollar below 117 yen after seeing the heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Friday," said Hideaki Furumaya, head of the interbank desk at Mizuho Trust & Banking. \par \par \uc2  Yen-buying pressure was strong as Wednesday is effectively the last \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading day ahead of interim fiscal book-closings on Friday, dealers said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  settlement takes place two business days after a transaction. \par \par \uc2  At 0550 GMT, the dollar was at 117.20/22 yen against 117.48 yen in late New York on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro stood at 108.22/30 yen , down from Tuesday's late New York level of 108.38 yen. \par \par \uc2  The market was also nervous about selling the euro against the yen after seeing the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the BOJ on Monday when Tokyo financial markets were closed for the Autumnal Equinox Day holiday. \par \par \uc2  The euro had fallen as low as 106.11 yen on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the euro barely moved, holding on to offshore gains to stand at $0.9235/40. \par \par \uc2  CONSUMER CONFIDENCE \par \par \uc2  The dollar managed to find support despite Tuesday's consumer confidence figures in September, which suffered the biggest one-month drop since October 1990 during the Gulf Crisis. \par \par \uc2  The private Conference Board said its monthly index of consumer confidence dropped 16.4 points to 97.6 in September from a month earlier, lower than forecast in a Reuters poll of economists. \par \par \uc2  The survey reflected only part of the shock of the attacks, which bodes ill for retail spending, which had been propping up the sluggish U.S. economy before the strikes. \par \par \uc2  Adding uncertainty were question marks over how Washington intends to retaliate for the assaults and what the economic impact of any action would be. \par \par \uc2  "Given that military action is imminent, there are growing risk factors facing U.S. assets," said Akihiro Nishida, chief economist at Tokyo-Mitsubishi Securities. \par \par \uc2  "But it's unclear whether there will be more repatriation from Japanese investors after the fiscal half-year end, since there aren't many attractive investment options at home." \par \par \uc2  LITTLE REACTION ON S&P \par \par \uc2  U.S. credit rating company Standard & Poor's said on Wednesday that it saw the September 11 attacks pushing the United States into recession in the third and fourth quarters. \par \par \uc2  S&P also said chances were increasing of a sharper downgrade of Japan's sovereign credit rating within the AA category, signalling that it may cut the rating more than a notch from its current double A-plus (AA+). \par \par \uc2  The rating company had already placed Japan's rating on a review for possible downgrade earlier in September and the dollar/yen rate showed no real reaction to the news. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0603 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2000 Cls\par                                 25 Sep.\par                        -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr              0.9231   0.9230   +0.01    -2.79   0.9496\par  Dlr/yen               117.22   117.48   -0.22    +2.42   114.45\par  Euro/yen              108.17   108.38   -0.19    -0.50   108.71\par  Stg/dlr               1.4720   1.4701   +0.13    -1.87   1.5000\par  Can/dlr               1.5698   1.5700   -0.01    +5.26   1.4914\par  Aus/dlr               0.4930   0.4927   +0.06   -11.87   0.5594\par  Euro/swiss            1.4650   1.4645   +0.03    -3.75   1.5221\par  Euro/stg              0.6269   0.6273   -0.06    -0.89   0.6325.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926dx9q033fh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
