\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar sits tight, wary of further BOJ action. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Charlotte Cooper \par \uc2 769 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2001\par 10:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 25 (Reuters) - The dollar sat tight in early European trade on Tuesday, steady against the euro but a quarter percent down on the yen, with traders wary that any attempt to push it lower could be met by the heavy hand of the Bank of Japan. \par \par \uc2  Hefty gains in U.S. stocks on Monday helped support the greenback but the market was bracing for U.S. consumer confidence data due at 1400 GMT, which includes figures from after the September 11 attacks on New York and Washington. \par \par \uc2  "It's a case of wait-and-see. We still have the underlying threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . People are reluctant to test the resolve of the central banks," said Mark Henry, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at GNI in London. \par \par \uc2  While the markets seemed calmer, analysts said the two main questions were what military action the U.S. was likely to take in response to the assaults and how the U.S. economy was faring. \par \par \uc2  The consumer confidence report was widely expected to show falling confidence as the strikes take their toll on sentiment. It could also signal a slowdown in retail spending, with concerns the U.S. economy, already sluggish before the attacks in the United States, is now threatening to tip into recession. \par \par \uc2  "Even if the report is better than expected, a rebound in the dollar should be pretty short-lived given the strains currently facing the U.S. economy," said Masanori Hirabayashi, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Shinsei Bank. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was down nearly a quarter of a percent against the yen at 117.27 by 0800 GMT but holding just above the sensitive 117 mark perceived by some to have been a level the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  wanted to defend in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday and last week. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was barely changed against the euro at $0.9168 but half a percent weaker against the Swiss franc at 1.5874 francs . It has rebounded about one percent from Friday's 20-month lows against the franc, with the Swiss National Bank prompted into lowering key interest rates on Monday to curb the attraction of the safe-haven franc. \par \par \uc2  STALWART DEFENCE \par \par \uc2  The dollar drew support on the apparent determination of Japanese monetary authorities to prevent an export-damaging rise in the yen. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan, acting on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , on Monday stepped in to sell the yen against the dollar and the euro in offshore trade. Tokyo financial markets were closed for Autumnal Equinox Day, a national holiday. \par \par \uc2  The move was the latest in a string of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It sold yen for dollars on three days last week, making a rare foray in both London and New York hours on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was slightly weaker against the yen at 107.50 , having rallied after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it had bought euros for yen on behalf of the BOJ on Monday. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had merely limited the yen's rise at best, doing little to change the downdraft for the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is working in a way to cap the yen's rallies, but not in a way to change the underlying trend," a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at a Japanese bank said. \par \par \uc2  "So far, the BOJ's aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is clearly helping to prevent the dollar from tumbling sharply. \par \par \uc2  "Without the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar would clearly have dropped below 115 yen by now." \par \par \uc2  STOCKS HELP DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  Sentiment for the dollar also picked up on Monday after sharp rallies on Wall Street, with the Dow Jones industrial average up 4.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  The Nasdaq Composite index rose about 5.4 percent. \par \par \uc2  But the market held its breath ahead of the release of the U.S. consumer confidence data. \par \par \uc2  Economists worry that the devastating attacks on the World Trade Center and the Pentagon will have dealt a tremendous blow to consumer sentiment. \par \par \uc2  Confidence had been slipping even before the attacks, hitting an eight-year low of 114.3 in August. \par \par \uc2  While the data for September will not reflect the full effects of the attacks, it will give markets their first taste of the impact. A Reuters poll of economists forecast the consumer confidence index would fall to 105.1. \par \par \uc2  Further ahead, Japanese Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi meets U.S. President George W. Bush later on Tuesday with the two heads of government expected to discuss efforts to ensure stability in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock markets and how to deal with money laundering. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926dx9p03cu2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
