\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  options - Euro vols down, confidence hits dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2001\par 20:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CHICAGO, Sept 25 (Reuters) - Implied volatility for short-dated euro options eased on Tuesday as the dollar sagged in the wake of weaker-than-expected consumer confidence data. \par \par \uc2  Volatility for one-month euro options was quoted at 13.15 percent, down from 13.2/13.4 percent on Monday. Volatility is a statistical measure of how much the options market expects the price of the underlying asset to move during the life of the option. \par \par \uc2  The euro/dollar rallied as high as $0.9248 after the confidence index came in at 97.6 in September, down from 114.0 in August. The data reflected the growing disenchantment with the U.S. economic outlook in the wake of the Sept. 11 attacks on U.S targets. Overall, options activity remained muted. \par \par \uc2  "Traders say the only trade of note was the purchase of an Oct. 18 $0.9150 put," said Tom Rogers, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at IFR \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Watch. \par \par \uc2  The 25-delta one-month risk reversal was quoted at 1.0 percent favoring euro calls, down from 1.1/1.3 percent on Monday. Risk reversals measure the volatility bias for out-of-the-money calls vs. puts. \par \par \uc2  Implied volatility for one-month yen options was quoted at 13.0 percent, near steady from 12.8/13.2 percent quoted on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen was trading just positive on Tuesday with traders reporting mild pressure from repatriation flows and lingering threats of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week and on Monday to weaken the yen against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The 25-delta one-month risk reversal was quoted at 1.95 percent favoring yen calls, compared with 1.9/2.1 percent favoring yen calls on Monday. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925dx9p0718x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
