\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2 's Europe  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  seen modest so far. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Dhara Ranasinghe \par \uc2 625 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2001\par 16:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 25 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foray into the foreign exchanges in European trading time has so far been moderate, analysts here said on Tuesday, with the Bank of Japan's tactics making a bigger impact on curbing yen strength. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan, acting on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has bought dollars and euros and sold yen over the past week to stem an export-damaging rise in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On Monday, it enlisted the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as its agent in European trading, sending a warning shot to the market that it wasn't afraid to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the clock. \par \par \uc2  A firm indication of how much \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent overall in the $1-trillion-a-day \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, as well as in Europe alone, is hard to glean until Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves data is released. \par \par \uc2  However, London traders estimate that Japan's bout of yen selling using the ECB on Monday was modest with one dealer putting the amount sold around 1.5 billion dollars worth of yen. \par \par \uc2  "So far, the overall \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been quite moderate by BOJ standards," said Ian Stannard, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas in London. \par \par \uc2  Estimates by European analysts of the total cost of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  which began on September 17 range between seven and 15 billion dollars, although some put the amount as high as $20 billion. \par \par \uc2  During January 1999 and April 2000, Japan spent around 120 billion dollars on weakening the yen. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ has shown in the past that it can be successful when it comes to preventing yen appreciation and will do as much as it needs to," Stannard said. \par \par \uc2  The yen has risen about five percent in the fortnight since the attacks on the United States, buoyed by risk aversion and a repatriation of foreign funds ahead of the September half-year end book closing. \par \par \uc2  It was trading around 117.35 per dollar at 1420 GMT, more than one percent below seven-month peaks set last week. While there has been no hint of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action on Tuesday, traders were wary that the BOJ was watching the market. \par \par \uc2  MORE BANG FOR THEIR BUCK \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that while they suspected the BOJ sold yen in small amounts on Monday, the change in Japan's tactics had a bigger impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "The key to what they've done is really the timing of it. They've offered clear verbal direction and then they've been prepared to back it up with actions," said Mark Henry, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at GNI in London. \par \par \uc2  "Somewhere around $10 billion would be the answer on the total (spent)." \par \par \uc2  Henry said he didn't think Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was overly sizeable. He added the BOJ had maximised the impact of its actions by letting dollar/yen slip last week and allowing stop-loss orders to build up. \par \par \uc2  This meant that when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again, automatic orders to buy dollar/yen were triggered on the upside. \par \par \uc2  The yen, which strengthened to around 116.25 before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, has subsequently shed almost a percent. \par \par \uc2  While it was not unusual for another \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to execute orders on behalf of the BOJ outside Tokyo hours, Monday's use of the ECB was also seen to mark a change in tactics. \par \par \uc2  "Yesterday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  via the ECB sent another signal to markets that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in other time zones," said Stannard from BNP Paribas. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  during European and U.S. trading time but dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seemed to have operated through banks' overnight desks in Tokyo. Monday, however was a holiday in Japan. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925dx9p053nj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
