\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  options - Yen vols soften after BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 2001\par 21:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CHICAGO, Sept 24 (Reuters) - Implied volatility for front-end yen options softened on Monday after the dollar/yen slumped in response to more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the yen's rise. \par \par \uc2  One-month yen options volatility eased to 12.8/13.2 percent, off from 13.7/14.0 percent at Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  Implied volatility is a statistical measure, expressed as a percentage, of how much the options market expects the price of the underlying asset to move during the life of the option. \par \par \uc2  The 25-delta one-month risk reversal for yen was near 1.9/2.1 percent favoring calls, near Friday's 2.1 percent. Risk reversals measure the volatility bias for out-of-the-money calls versus puts. \par \par \uc2  "They're trying to put a floor in the dollar/yen around 116.00," said one \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  options trader. "It ought to bring the risk reversals in, because it's limiting the downside risk you have. (But) that doesn't mean it can't blow through there. If you trade dollar/yen enough, (you know) they're not always successful." \par \par \uc2  The BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight was the latest in a series of actions that began last week. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold yen for dollars on three days last week. \par \par \uc2  The trader noted that the dollar/yen price action signaled that the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have had greater impact on Monday than in the recent past, as the dollar hung near session highs. \par \par \uc2  "Today is the first day that there hasn't been a sharp retracement after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. "It's been able to hold the gains, which is fairly significant. \par \par \uc2  As for one-month euro options, volatility was at 13.2/13.4 percent from a 13.6 percent close on Friday. The risk reversal was 1.1/1.3 percent favoring calls, compared with 1.4 percent on Friday. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010924dx9o012fg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
