\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen rocked anew by BOJ, SNB cut hits Swiss franc. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Natsuko Waki \par \uc2 795 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 2001\par 14:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 24 (Reuters) - The yen shed three quarters of a percent against the dollar on Monday as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb its export-damaging strength, while the Swiss franc also fell against the greenback after Switzerland cut its interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The yen racked up greater losses against the euro, falling a full one percent as traders cited talk the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also in the market buying euros for yen on behalf of Japan. \par \par \uc2  The ECB declined to comment, butJapan's top financial diplomat Haruhiko Kuroda said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in appropriate \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  including the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "There were rumours of ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and we saw euro/dollar shoot up... We saw euro/yen jump up first so it could be them on behalf of the Bank of Japan," said Neil Parker, market strategist at RBS Financial Markets. \par \par \uc2  Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  marked the latest action by the BOJ which began last week. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold yen for dollars on three days last week and it even \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in both London and New York hours on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The euro rose as high as 107.90 yen from 106.55 in late New York on Friday. The greenback rose in tandem with the euro, but the scale of the rise was still limited given persistent sales by Japanese exporters and investors. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier lifted the dollar to session highs of 117.55 yen, up more than one percent from its seven-month lows of 115.76 hit last week in the wake of aerial attacks on the United States on September 11. \par \par \uc2  "There is no doubt the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is having some stabilising effect. Today's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not just a reassurance of their presence but definitely communicated their seriousness to the market," said Joe Prendergast, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy and research at Credit Suisse First Boston. \par \par \uc2  The euro erased earlier losses to firm against the dollar, highs of $0.9204. \par \par \uc2  The Swiss franc retreated from Friday's 20-month highs against the dollar to stand nearly one percent down at 1.5920 per dollar after the Swiss National Bank cut its benchmark interest rate target half a percentage point to 1.75-2.75 percent, citing concerns about recent franc strength. \par \par \uc2  The franc had gained more than seven percent since September 11, despite a previous interest rate cut a week ago. \par \par \uc2  DOGGED DEFENCE \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the BOJ looked determined to defend the 115 yen level, where many Japanese companies set their internal rates. \par \par \uc2  "With stock markets falling, exporters are having difficulty. If the dollar goes lower than 115, that means most of them will be in real trouble," a European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Japan's benchmark Nikkei average is languishing near 17-year lows as uncertainty over U.S. military action fuels fears of a drop in consumer spending and dampened exports. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in both London and New York hours, with dealers estimating the total amount purchased by the BOJ could be upwards of $10 billion - making it more than that bought during Monday and Wednesday combined. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said last week he had asked the BOJ to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds unsterilised, which means leaving them in the banking system rather than draining them out as per its usual practice. \par \par \uc2  Unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  creates a surplus in the money market and increases downward pressure on interest rates. \par \par \uc2  "In a way, Japan is loosening its monetary policy by buying dollars in unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , injecting more liquidity to the system," Lee Ferridge, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Rabobank said. \par \par \uc2  Pressure is piling up on the BOJ to ease yet more with the the economy being dealt a double blow from faltering stock markets and the yen strength. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its discount rate to 0.1 percent last Tuesday as part of concerted global interest rate cuts following the attacks in New York and Washington on September 11. \par \par \uc2  Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  jitters, some dealers said a potential reversal in the dollar's fortunes could encourage technically-driven funds to sell dollars for yen, accelerating the dollar's slide. \par \par \uc2  "Speculators like model funds are still biased to the higher dollar/yen, but if the dollar breaks 115 yen those guys could start selling dollars massively," another European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Investors were keeping an eye on Wall Street to see how it opens later in the day. Last week, U.S. stock markets suffered their biggest weekly loss since the Great Depression in the 1930s, with the Dow Jones industrial average falling 14 percent in just five sessions. The Nasdaq December futures was up 36 points by 1200 GMT. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010924dx9o00pxp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
