\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2-BOJ drafts in ECB as agent for  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 727 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 2001\par 18:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 24 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to weaken the yen at least twice on Monday and on the second occasion enlisted the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to act as its agent in Europe. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times in Asian, European and U.S. trading hours in the last week to try to push the yen down. But traders said the latest round of yen selling, which appeared to be for euros rather than dollars, and via the ECB, marked a new approach. \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat Haruhiko Kuroda told Reuters after Monday's second round of yen selling, which sent the euro and the dollar soaring, that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was being conducted in "appropriate \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 " and not just the dollar. \par \par \uc2  With Japanese markets on holiday, traders at once suspected that the ECB might be acting on behalf of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Asked whether the ECB was involved in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , an ECB spokesman initally said only "No comment". But a few hours later, the ECB released a statement confirming it had bought euros for yen on behalf of the Bank of Japan. \par \par \uc2  "ECB confirms that in line with the agency agreement that it has with the Bank of Japan, it has been buying euros against the yen on behalf of the Bank of Japan," an ECB spokesman said, giving no further details about the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Despite the ECB's assistance, London traders were quick to point out that this should not be seen as coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the euro zone authorities. \par \par \uc2  "The ECB is just processing the BOJ's orders. They're not acting for themselves," said a trader at a U.S. bank in London. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ had also stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets earlier in the London morning. \par \par \uc2  "Today, under instruction by Finance Minister (Masajuro) Shiokawa, we have taken appropriate action in the exchange market," Kuroda told Reuters after the first action. \par \par \uc2  He also warned that Japan would continue to take appropriate action as necessary to preserve exchange rate stability. \par \par \uc2  The yen has been strengthening in recent days on repatriation flows. Investors worldwide have been pulling out of riskier assets because they are concerned about the market impact of probable U.S. military action following the attacks on its cities. \par \par \uc2  Japan first began its current campaign to lower the yen last Monday in a bid to help its exporters at a time when the economy is already on the brink of its fourth recession in a decade. \par \par \uc2  "Japan seems to have drawn a line in the sand at 117 to the dollar," said Steven Saywell, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank in London. \par \par \uc2  "Brief blips beyond this level are not a problem but the government does not want to see this happen for any sustained period because of the implications for the Japanese economy." \par \par \uc2  Traders noted that the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Monday was conducted during the Asian trading session but later in the week it had also acted in both the London and New York sessions. \par \par \uc2  Many speculated that Friday's bout of yen selling for dollars during the U.S. session was conducted by Japanese banks' overnight desks in Tokyo rather than through agents in New York. \par \par \uc2  Traders have estimated that the BOJ spent roughly $7 to 8 billion of yen at the beginning of last week and maybe as much as $10 billion of yen on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the BOJ's action last week only put a cap on further yen gains as Japan is seen to be swimming against the tide in the $1 trillion a day \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The Swiss National Bank has also been struggling to try and lower its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which has soared since the September 11 attacks on New York and Washington. \par \par \uc2  Last Friday, it guided interest rates on its securities repurchase agreements down to reflect its concern about the franc's rapid appreciation. \par \par \uc2  But on Monday, it was forced to cut its key interest rate target by 50 basis points, only one week after it made a similar cut in conjunction with several other major central banks. \par \par \uc2  At 1545 GMT, the dollar was up three quarters of a percent on the day, trading around 117.45 yen , and the euro was up by a similar degree at 107.32 yen . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010924dx9o00pxf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
