\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Sour after Japan seizes chance to weaken yen again. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,387 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 2001\par 11:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Sept 24 (Reuters) - Most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  headed south late on Monday after the yen fell a quarter \par \par \uc2  of a percent against the dollar and the euro on \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ). \par \par \uc2      Trade was relatively choppy in the regionals as they \par \par \uc2  tracked movements in the yen, which had strengthened against \par \par \uc2  the dollar earlier in the day amid hefty buying orders. \par \par \uc2      Confirmation the BOJ had taken steps to weaken the \par \par \uc2  export-crimping yen came as top financial diplomat Haruhiko \par \par \uc2  Kuroda said appropriate action had been taken in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2      Suspicion the BOJ might make such a move had been running \par \par \uc2  high throughout the day given the closure of Japanese stock \par \par \uc2  markets for a one-day Autumnal Equinox Day holiday. \par \par \uc2      Apart from the influence of dollar/yen, the mood remained \par \par \uc2  cautious despite a tentative recovery in many Asian stock \par \par \uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2      The threat of a global recession drew ever closer as the \par \par \uc2  United States continued to plan its response to the September \par \par \uc2  11 attacks, feared to have killed nearly 7,000 people. \par \par \uc2      Analysts have stressed that despite initial weakness in \par \par \uc2  the \par \par \uc2   dollar following the attacks, Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were bound to \par \par \uc2  trend lower given heightened worries over the region's economic \par \par \uc2  prospects. \par \par \uc2      South Korea lowered its 2001 forecast for gross domestic \par \par \uc2  product (GDP) on Sunday to just two to three percent \par \par \uc2  year-on-year. The Finance Ministry had previously projected \par \par \uc2  growth of four percent. \par \par \uc2      Hong Kong looked set to follow after Financial Secretary \par \par \uc2  Antony Leung said the government would cut its growth forecast, \par \par \uc2  which currently stands at one percent year-on-year. \par \par \uc2      Volatility was seen keeping to a minimum in Asia's \par \par \uc2  relatively illiquid \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, however, given expectations \par \par \uc2  some central banks would be waiting in the wings to give \par \par \uc2  guidance to their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht edged lower after onshore banks, corporates and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offshore funds bought the majors either to cover positions or\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par repatriate money to Japan ahead of the end-September book\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par closings.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But the baht's downside was limited by dollar sales linked\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to a foreign company's planned acquisition of a local company.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Mexican cement maker Cemex              , the world's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par third-biggest cement maker, is likely to take a stake of more\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par than 50 percent in TPIP soon, a company source said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said a company linked to the deal sold a sizeable\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par amount of dollars into the market on Monday, but it was not\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par clear if the money came from the asset sales.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso advanced against the dollar, threatening to break\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par above the key 51.00 mark on the back of capital inflows from a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign cement manufacturer into the local unit.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso closed at 51.185 against an open of 51.320 in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par brisk trade, with market turnover of $104.75 million compared\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with $19.50 million in the previous session.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The inflows from that company basically dominated the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market today. Otherwise, there were small transactions here and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par there," said a Manila dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In the money market, the Treasury accepted an average rate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of 9.577 percent for 91-day T-bills at its auction earlier on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Monday, against last week's 9.467 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But National Treasurer Sergio Edeza said he expected T-bill\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rates to be flat to lower at the next week's auction.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar fell to levels not seen since well before\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the September 11 attacks after the BOJ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Prior to confirmation the BOJ had been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sing had been driven substantially lower amid talk some players\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par were unwinding yen/Sing carry trades to take profits at current\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par levels.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The effects of a weaker U.S. dollar in the days following\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the attacks on the United States wore thin, with analysts\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expecting the Sing to remain soft given the city state's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par heightened economic worries.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par There were no signs the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might have been\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par orchestrating U.S. dollar purchases via local banks as it was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par suspected to have done last week, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won ended at a two-month low after a sharp fall in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par non-deliverable forwards (NDF) market gave a boost to the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sizeable dollar sales by a state-run bank to lift the won\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par off intraday lows of around 1,308 per dollar only had a limited\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par impact.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won had generally been on the rise since early April\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par amid hopes for foreign investment inflows, but the rise has\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par been blocked by a shaky yen and worries over the local economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the NDF market, the one-month won edged down to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,308.9/09.9 versus 1,307.7/08.7 earlier and three-month won to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,311.7/12.7 versus 1,311.3/12.3.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah continued to hover at the wrong side of 9,400\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par per dollar but was a comfortable way off recent lows of around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 9,700.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Trade remained thin and driven by genuine commercial needs\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as would-be players remained cautious on how the United States\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would react to the recent attacks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Prospects for credit easing in Indonesia looked even more\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par distant after the country's statistics bureau warned inflation\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par below 10 percent would be almost impossible to achieve in 2001\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unless the price of goods could be contained in the coming\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weeks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Year-on-year inflation hit 12.23 percent in August from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 13.04 percent a month earlier - the second fall this year but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par still high enough to worry economists and thwart attempts to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bring punitive interest rates down.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Indonesia has targeted inflation of 9.3 percent under the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2001 state budget.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Finance Ministry said it expected Indonesia's capital\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par account deficit to fall sharply in the second half compared to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the first half mainly due to bigger loan receipts.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar ended lower following U.S. dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par purchases in the non-delivery forwards market spurred by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par jitters over the domestic stock market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Taiwan said they expected the Taiwan dollar to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par continue feeling the pressure of falling stocks and possible\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign fund outflows on Tuesday, and that the domestic\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could trade in a T$34.500-T$34.700 band.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had been trading in a tight range since the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market resumed trading last Wednesday following a devastating\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par typhoon which shut down the island for two days.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0844 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     117.19       116.28         -0.78\par  Sing dlr      1.7550       1.7430         -0.68\par  Taiwan dlr    34.578       34.573         -0.01\par  Korean won   1307.70      1295.00         -0.97\par  Baht           44.39        44.15         -0.54\par  Peso           51.17        51.19         +0.04\par  Rupiah       9485.00      9410.00         -0.79\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.19       102.21        -12.78\par  Sing dlr      1.7550       1.6640         -5.19\par  Taiwan dlr    34.578       31.380         -9.25\par  Korean won   1307.70      1135.00        -13.21\par  Baht           44.39        37.45        -15.63\par  Peso           51.17        40.20        -21.44\par  Rupiah       9485.00      6975.00        -26.46\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.8000         +0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------ ASIAN STOCK\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MARKETS  0844 GMT\par