\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ New York Bank Manager Can't Comment On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 192 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2001\par 16:19\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's New York general manager couldn't comment Friday on reports that the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in New York in a bid to weaken the yen. \par \par \uc2  "I have no comment on that," said Yasu Maehara. \par \par \uc2  Reached at temporary offices, Maehara referred any questions on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which makes any decisions on whether the BOJ should step into the market. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ has decamped to temporary offices in New York in the wake of last week's attacks on the World Trade Center. \par \par \uc2  "We are operating in temporary offices, we can't comment on that," Maehara added. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official reached in New York also couldn't comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk, referring questions to Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets aggressively during Asian trading hours and was also reported to have acted during London trading in an ongoing bid to halt the appreciation of the yen. \par \par \uc2  -By Grainne McCarthy, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-2381; grainne.mccarthy@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1074 4164 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010921dx9l000v7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
