\par\par \b \uc2  MOF Kuroda: Confirms  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Friday \b0\par\par\uc2 111 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2001\par 04:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat, Haruhiko Kuroda, confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry Of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Bank Of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Friday. \par \par \uc2  "We took appropriate action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets today," Kuroda said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 0248 GMT, the dollar/yen was trading at 117.30.\par - - 21/09/01 02-51G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar sank to a seven-month low against the yen overnight,\par hitting an intraday low in the U.S. of Y115.82, its weakest point\par against the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since Feb 26.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929;\par miyako.takebe@dowjones.com\par -0- 21/09/01 03-08G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010921dx9l00049\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
