\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian dollar rises in early dealings. \b0\par\par\uc2 590 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2001\par 16:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      Bank of Canada: CANADA OPEN  1.5677  PREVIOUS CLOSE 1.5708 \par \par \uc2  -------------------------------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2      TORONTO, Sept 21 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar improved \par \par \uc2  on Friday, as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the yen helped the \par \par \uc2  greenback, and some merger-and-acquisition flows were also seen \par \par \uc2  as supportive. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar was at C$1.5660 to the U.S. dollar, or \par \par \uc2  63.86 U.S. cents, up from Thursday's Bank of Canada official \par \par \uc2  closing rate of C$1.5708 to the U.S. dollar, or 63.66 U.S. \par \par \uc2  cents. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had opened stronger at C$1.5677. \par \par \uc2  "There's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in dollar-yen, that's forcing the \par \par \uc2  dollar higher there. Some are saying if the (U.S.) dollar is \par \par \uc2  doing well against everything, the Canadian dollar should do \par \par \uc2  okay," said Andy Busch, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  advisor at BMO \par \par \uc2  Nesbitt Burns in Chicago. \par \par \uc2  Overnight, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push the \par \par \uc2  greenback up three-quarters of a yen after it sagged to the \par \par \uc2  day's low near 116. It was the third day this week the Japanese \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to restrain the yen. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, market players were waiting to see how U.S. \par \par \uc2  equities would fare after European equity markets sold off \par \par \uc2  sharply because President George W. Bush warned on Thursday \par \par \uc2  that a lengthy war on terrorism was imminent. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones industrial average fell more than 3 percent, \par \par \uc2  while the Nasdaq shed more than 5 percent amid uncertainty over \par \par \uc2  what a protracted U.S. war against terrorism will mean for the \par \par \uc2  slumping economy and corporate profits. Toronto stocks followed \par \par \uc2  their U.S. counterparts lower, losing 3 percent. \par \par \uc2  Fears of a rush into recession have bruised North American \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after last week's attacks in the United States \par \par \uc2  shattered already-frail consumer confidence. \par \par \uc2  Since Canada and the United States share a trading \par \par \uc2  partnership worth more than $1 billion a day, Canada's ability \par \par \uc2  to skirt the effects of the attacks seems limited. \par \par \uc2  With prospect of recession hanging in the air, the Canadian \par \par \uc2  dollar looked to be headed to test the all-time low of \par \par \uc2  C$1.5850, but some say merger and acquisition related flows \par \par \uc2  have tempered its slide, providing a little bit stability. \par \par \uc2  Late on Thursday, U.S.-based Duke Energy Corp. said it will \par \par \uc2  acquire Canada's Westcoast Energy Inc. for $3.5 billion in a \par \par \uc2  cash-and-stock deal. \par \par \uc2  It is the second major deal this month involving Canadian \par \par \uc2  and U.S. energy firms. Earlier, U.S.-based Devon Energy's \par \par \uc2  purchase of Canadian oil and gas firm Anderson Exploration may \par \par \uc2  be delaying the Canadian dollar's decline. Both deals are seen \par \par \uc2  as supportive for the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because it means the \par \par \uc2  acquirer will need to buy Canadian dollars to pay for its \par \par \uc2  purchase. \par \par \uc2  The market is waiting for remarks from Bank of Canada \par \par \uc2  Governor David Dodge on Friday. He had canceled a speech \par \par \uc2  earlier this week due to travel disruptions in the wake of last \par \par \uc2  week's deadly attacks. His remarks will be posted on the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Web site at 1 p.m. (1700 GMT). \par \par \uc2  Overnight, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ranged between C$1.5635 and \par \par \uc2  C$1.5720. It improved in early North American dealings to \par \par \uc2  C$1.5625 and C$1.5679. \par \par \uc2  In cross-trading, the Canadian dollar was at 74.45 \par \par \uc2  yen , compared with 73.98 yen at the previous close, and \par \par \uc2  at C$1.4359 to the euro versus C$1.4571. Against the \par \par \uc2  Australian dollar it was at A$1.3124 versus A$1.2906. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010921dx9l00nmk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
