\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2 's MoF confirms  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2  in New York. \b0\par\par\uc2 124 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2001\par 15:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 21 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it confirmed the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BoJ) is acting as its agent and is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the New York \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by buying dollars for yen. \par \par \uc2  "We can confirm that the BoJ is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  now in New York," a finance ministry official told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  At 1335 GMT the yen was quoted at 116.50 to the dollar, compared with an earlier high of 116.04 yen, according to Reuters data. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times this week to curb strength in the yen. Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa confirmed on Friday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had conducted solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010921dx9l00n5k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
