\par\par \b \uc2  MOF Kuroda: To Take Appropriate  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Steps As Needed \b0\par\par\uc2 278 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 September 2001\par 02:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Japan's top financial diplomat said Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry Of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to take the proper steps when necessary against any excessive strengthening of the yen. \par \par \uc2  "We will take appropriate (\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) steps as needed," Haruhiko Kuroda said when asked by reporters whether the MOF will continue to take measures against the strong yen. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda, the vice finance minister for international affairs, said Japanese authorities are closely watching \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  The MOF ordered the Bank Of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to buy the dollar for yen Monday and again Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  At 0045 GMT Thursday, the dollar was at Y117.51, just down from Y117.54 late Wednesday in New York, but above Y117.34 in London on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda confirmed that he received instructions from Japan's Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa to go to Europe and the U.S. to discuss the upcoming meeting of finance officials from the Group of Seven major industrialized nations. \par \par \uc2  However, Kuroda declined to comment on his trip to Europe and the U.S. and on the planned topics for the G7 meeting. \par \par \uc2  He also said he hadn't yet heard any details from the U.S., the host of the next meeting, about where the meeting would be held. \par \par \uc2  The G7 finance ministers' meeting was originally scheduled to be held in Washington, D.C. in late September, but last week's terrorist strikes on the World Trade Center and the Pentagon have increased the possibility of the meeting's location being moved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By Ron Harui; Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929;\par ronharui@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010920dx9k00012\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
