\par\par \b \uc2  MOF Shiokawa: To Dispatch Kuroda To Europe To Discuss G7 \b0\par\par\uc2 467 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2001\par 12:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said Wednesday he will dispatch Deputy Vice Finance Minister Haruhiko Kuroda to Europe and the U.S. to discuss the upcoming meeting of finance ministers from the Group of Seven nations. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa said he hadn't heard any details from the U.S., the host of the next meeting, about where the meeting would be held. \par \par \uc2  The G7 finance ministers meeting was originally scheduled to be held in Washington, D.C. in late September, but last week's terrorist strikes on the World Trade Center and the Pentagon have raised the possibility of the meeting's location being moved. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa said Kuroda will be going on the trip to Europe and the U.S. "soon." \par \par \uc2  "I think there is a need to hear out the U.S. opinion (about G7). As for Europe, a working level meeting there has been canceled. And the IMF meeting has been called off too," Shiokawa said. \par \par \uc2  "There is no set purpose for his trip. The point is simply just to be in contact" with other countries, Shiokawa said. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa noted that a working level meeting of European countries in London scheduled for Sept. 23 had been canceled. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa added he expects Japan will be able to count on help from its rich country partners to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem the yen's rise in the event \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unable to contain market fluctuations that may result as a reaction to any U.S. retaliation to last week's terrorist attacks. \par \par \uc2  "If it comes to that, yes, I think we there will be international cooperation," Shiokawa said. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa was coy about whether MOF directed the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Wednesday afternoon as rumored, though he strongly implied the ministry did. \par \par \uc2  "You should be able to tell just by looking," Shiokawa said. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa added the MOF asked the BOJ at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy board meeting Tuesday to leave excess funds from \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market and not "sterilize" the funds as is customary. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually "sterilizes" its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by using money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to absorb back from banks the yen it sold to them in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Leaving the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsterilized would put downward pressure on the yen. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ didn't enter the money market at its usual \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  time of 0020 GMT Wednesday, effectively leaving funds from Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  MOF also asked the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep its bank reserve target over Y8 trillion, which the bank has done, said Shiokawa. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   -By Audrey McAvoy, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929;\par audrey.mcavoy@dowjones.com\par -0- 19/09/01 10-37G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010919dx9j000nx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
