\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Soars Vs Yen After BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  Again \b0\par\par\uc2  By Ron Harui \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 408 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2001\par 09:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar soared more than a yen in Asia Wednesday after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second time this week, spurring speculation that Japanese authorities will continue to put a floor under the embattled U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered the market just as the dollar threatened to fall below key support at Y117.10. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which market participants estimated to be worth several hundred million dollars - roughly the same scale as Monday's action - sent the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flying to a high of Y118.12. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said Japan was in close contact with U.S. and European authorities when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday, though \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  acted alone, and warned that the ministry was ready to take steps again if needed. \par \par \uc2  "I have said we will be closely monitoring markets and taking appropriate action, as we did today," Shiokawa told reporters soon after he ordered the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to act. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  soon after its daily money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in which it left excess yen from Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  flooding the market - effectively leaving Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "unsterilized." \par \par \uc2  Leaving \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsterilized was unprecedented for the BOJ, which has always soaked up excess funds from the market two days after past \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Ron Leven, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Lehman Brothers, said this could signal the beginning of a "sea change" in Japanese policy. If the ministry keeps \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  - and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  leaves the excess yen in the market - Japanese authorities could put a floor under the dollar, Leven said. \par \par \uc2  That means all eyes will be on the BOJ's money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday morning to see if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  leaves Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsterilized. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (0:15 a.m. EST), the dollar was quoted at Y117.72, above Y117.23 late Tuesday in New York. The dollar was at Y117.94 late Tuesday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $0.9256, lower than $0.9279 late Tuesday in New York. The euro was at $0.9200 in Tokyo Tuesday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y108.96, up from Y108.78 in\par New York late Tuesday. The euro was at Y108.51 in Tokyo late Tuesday.\par -0- 19/09/01 07-00G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010919dx9j000df\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
