\par\par \b \uc2  Shiokawa: More  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  If Needed, Watching Mkts \b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2001\par 04:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  acted alone in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  He said, however, the ministry is in touch with the U.S. and European nations with regard to Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The possibility of joint action in the future, however, would depend on the circumstances, he said. possible future cooperation in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I have said we will be closely monitoring markets and taking appropriate action, as we did today," he told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  (Corrected at 0722GMT) \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa said the ministry will continue to watch \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets closely and take action as needed. \par \par \uc2  He also suggested the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will leave the funds from Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  Asked whether comments from BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami meant the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  intends to leave \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds unsterilized, Shiokawa said only, "The BOJ is acting along those lines." \par \par \uc2  Hayami said Tuesday, "The bank will use all money, including that used for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in order to provide ample liquidity to the market." \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa declined to say how much yen was sold in Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The action is the second this week by the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities. Right after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around 0147 GMT, the dollar jumped from around Y117.12 to Y117.86. \par \par \uc2  At 0254 GMT, the dollar was changing hands at Y117.85. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa also said he welcomed the BOJ's decision to ease policy Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Audrey McAvoy, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; audrey.mcavoy@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said Japan was in contact with U.S. and European authorities with regards to Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The possibility of joint action in the future, however, would depend on the circumstances, he said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (An item that ran around 0228 GMT misstated the nature of Japan's\par contact with the U.S. and European authorities.)\par -0- 19/09/01 07-22G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010919dx9j00047\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
